codemap 9
tour feature-open-diff-row
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The Diff tab lists every tour added (+), removed (-) or changed (~) against the parent revision's map (@- in jj, HEAD in git), with a summary of what changed and, for changed tours, a line per new or changed step. The owner reaches for it to audit what a session changed in the map and whether it mapped what it built. Clicking a row opens that tour in the document; a removed tour, which exists only in the parent, is described in the status bar instead. 'refresh' reads the parent's map again, for when the parent revision moved.

